.TH AD_DEBUG 1 "2026-09-10" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_debug \- interactive pipeline debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_debug
.RI [ options ] " <oldfile> " <newfile>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_debug
takes an old and new file, runs the full ad_vim pipeline
(compute \(-> postprocess \(-> pace \(-> animator) stage by stage,
prints diagnostic information to the terminal, AND writes the
intermediate output of each stage to disk under
.I /tmp/ad_debug/
so you can inspect it with any external tool (less, cat -A, diff, wc,
etc.).
.PP
Stage files produced:
.TP
.I /tmp/ad_debug/raw.txt
Stage 1 (ad_compute output)
.TP
.I /tmp/ad_debug/post.txt
Stage 2 (ad_postprocess output)
.TP
.I /tmp/ad_debug/timed.txt
Stage 3 (ad_layer_pace output)
.TP
.I /tmp/ad_debug/snap.txt
Stage 4 (ad final buffer)
.PP
The script then compares the animator's final buffer (snap.txt)
against the new file and reports either a MATCH or a MISMATCH (printing
the diff in the latter case).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show detailed help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Do not clear
.I /tmp/ad_debug/
before running. Useful when you want to compare stage files across runs.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <oldfile>
Path to the original/source file (initial buffer).
.TP
.I <newfile>
Path to the target file the animation should produce.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_debug old.py new.py
Run the full pipeline and report MATCH/MISMATCH.
.TP
.B ad_debug \-\-keep old.py new.py
Keep previous stage files for comparison.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_vim (1),
.BR ad_pipeline (1),
.BR ad_snapshot (1)
